Z||000003||Nashco||12-09-2001||01:38 AM||||Oh yeah..and these (for sale if you're interested):<BR> <A HREF="http://home1.gte.net/jbnash/fiero/clearlights/leftside.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://home1.gte.net/jbnash/fiero/clearlights/leftside.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://home1.gte.net/jbnash/fiero/clearlights/rightside.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://home1.gte.net/jbnash/fiero/clearlights/rightside.jpg</A> <P>Another very easy alternative is to just remove the reflective lense/diffuser and install colored bulbs for a fake clear style.<P>Also, the <A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com/" TARGET=_blank>Fibersmith</A> has some cool fiberglass GT replacements.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||SLAMMED87GT||12-09-2001||12:12 PM||||Here's a picture of mine. I took at the diffusers, polished the lense really good. Then I bought PolarG bulbs at $10 a piece to replace the other ones. These are the really good ones, the ricers use them. They are acutally red glass, not the dipped bulbs that fade and look like crap.<P>So after I put those together This is what it looks like! <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero10-01,5.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pfierosig2_1.jpg"> <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto450 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||6
Z||000005||Spektrum-87GT||12-09-2001||03:41 PM||||slammed: you've got some awesome tail lights... whats a diffusor? i dont want to be a copycat, but they're awesome, details on how you did it please!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/spektrum_87gt/" TARGET=_blank>87 Fiero GT</A><BR>1991 Jeep Cherokee<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://members.home.com/bspracklin1/sig2.jpg">   <BR>AIM:<FONT COLOR="red">S</FONT><FONT COLOR="purple">p</FONT><FONT COLOR="blue">e</FONT><FONT COLOR="cyan">k</FONT><FONT COLOR="green">t</FONT><FONT COLOR="yellow">r</FONT><FONT COLOR="orange">u</FONT><FONT COLOR="red">m</FONT><FONT COLOR="purple">1</FONT><FONT COLOR="blue">1</FONT><FONT COLOR="cyan">7</FONT><BR>And no! i'm not gay dangit!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Nashco||12-09-2001||04:15 PM||||The diffusers are the red and orange plastic parts inside your taillight lenses that have those black lines running through them.  They spread the light so it doesn't just have one bright spot from the bulb.<P>Slammed, what'd you use to polish your lenses?  That's one thing that sucks on my lenses is that they are kind of scuffed up and have some sort of chemical stain/streak in one spot.  Yours look like glass almost!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||85ZainoGT||12-09-2001||05:13 PM||||slammed -- that is what I had started doing, butI cant find a good enough polish... what did u use?  and where did you buy all your stuff to do it? thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 GT all the options :)<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpicNEW3bsmall2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||MinnGreenGT||12-10-2001||10:08 AM||||3M makes a "clear plastic polish" that I picked up from the local auto parts place for about $7.  I think Wizard's also makes a clear plastic polish. Stuff works great (even if you're not doing the clear taillights).<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
