Z||000010||Rare87GT||12-10-2001||04:40 PM||||That looks sweet man.  I really like the look of those tailights. <P>------------------<BR>1987 GT (Maroon)*5 Speed*<BR>(Canadian Car)<BR>2.8L Mods--No Cat, K&N||||reg||1
Z||000011||SLAMMED87GT||12-11-2001||01:14 AM||||To those that were curious to what kind of polish I used, its actually made by Turtle Wax. It can be used on more than just plastic as well! It's not very expensive and cleaned them up pretty nice.<P>The bulbs are called "PolorG". They are available online at the ricer stores. I bought mine from a rice store in the area.<P>DO NOT buy dipped bulbs. They are junk. Even if it looks good when you first buy them, they will fade or be discolored after a little while. Spend the extra money (yep, $10 a bulb!) and get quality bulbs.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pfierosig2_1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto450 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||6
Z||000012||NOCONES||12-11-2001||01:27 AM||||I don't think you should say ricer stores like your above them....  i mean your car is exaclty like a riced out civic except yours looked good to begin with.  otherwise there the same.  I'm just having trouble with your logic that you shop at these stores, yet refer to them as RICE stores like there the plauge..  not intended to flame or defimate your car, but i'm just trying to understand the antirice mind.  I personaly love your car.  but i'm just wondering what makes everyone else rice and you not?||||reg||1
Z||000013||Nashco||12-11-2001||09:11 AM||||He never said anything bad about the rice store, and he's obviously not talking as if he's above them...<P>The rice store is where you buy things like stickers, big wings, seatbelt pads, tint, clear lights, bulbs, neons, gauges, gauge faces, shift knobs, pedal covers, etc.  You know, the stuff that the ricers use.  It was a generic term for whatever your local "compact car tuner" store is called.<P>Chill...<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000014||MinnGreenGT||12-11-2001||10:23 AM||||Just to add to the above info... you can now pick up LED bulbs for your taillights through JC Whitney's Sport & Compact section.  They are APC bulbs and only run $10 ea! (thanks Nashco for locating these)<P>And as to the Ricer comment.  I agree with Nascho... it really isn't meant to be a negative comment when used as above.  Just descriptive (not your normal "checker auto") and it's easier than saying something PC lile "import auto enthusiast's retail location"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
